velops, manufactures, and markets medical equipment for the management of diabetes. The company offers technologies including insulin delivery devices, such as insulin pumps and pens, continuous glucose monitors, other consumables, supplies, and related software and services. It serves people with diabetes who require insulin therapy, which represents all people with T1D and a subset of those with T2D. The company's platform includes Automated Insulin Delivery (AID) systems for glucose sensing and automated insulin dosing and administration for glycemic control and Smart Multiple Daily Injection (MDI) systems for self-administering insulin by manual injections, which include InPen, Simplera Sync, or Guardian 4 sensor, and wraparound applications and services. It also offers CareLink, a software platform that provides support for person with diabetes, their caretakers, and HCPS. MiniMed Group, Inc. was founded in 1983 and is headquartered in Northridge, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Que Thanh Dallara | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $388K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["MiniMed Group, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.7B market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 54% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $420M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield